  {
    "page": 1,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 681,
    "width": 920,
    "height": 14,
    "label": "EDITION 04 / AN ATLAS OF LIVED FUTURES"
  },
  {
    "page": 1,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 706,
    "width": 345,
    "height": 64.8,
    "label": "Worlds we\ncan inhabit"
  },
  {
    "page": 1,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 400,
    "top": 700,
    "width": 560,
    "height": 35.8,
    "label": "Walk into five possible ways of living. Follow the paths, join the experiences, and look inside the architecture that sustains them. These are worlds people could choose to build together."
  },
  {
    "page": 1,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 400,
    "top": 778,
    "width": 560,
    "height": 11,
    "label": "A worldbuilding project by Ren, developed with AI"
  },
  {
    "page": 2,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 802,
    "width": 920,
    "height": 10,
    "label": "WORLDS WE CAN INHABIT / EDITION 04"
  },
  {
    "page": 2,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 920,
    "top": 802,
    "width": 40,
    "height": 10,
    "label": "02 / 25"
  },
  {
    "page": 2,
    "kind": "image",
    "x": 0,
    "top": 0,
    "width": 1000,
    "height": 666.6666666666666,
    "label": "assets-v3/production-commons.png"
  },
  {
    "page": 2,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 681,
    "width": 920,
    "height": 14,
    "label": "THE MEANS TO BEGIN / PRODUCTIVE CAPACITY"
  },
  {
    "page": 2,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 706,
    "width": 345,
    "height": 64.8,
    "label": "Imagination\nacquires machinery"
  },
  {
    "page": 2,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 400,
    "top": 700,
    "width": 560,
    "height": 71.6,
    "label": "Robots, tools, materials, and shared knowledge give an idea a route into the world. Existing automated factories already manufacture robots and industrial equipment. [E1] [E2] This scene imagines that capacity organized for common provision and further construction, so the freedom to make worlds rests on a working material foundation."
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 802,
    "width": 920,
    "height": 10,
    "label": "WORLDS WE CAN INHABIT / EDITION 04"
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 920,
    "top": 802,
    "width": 40,
    "height": 10,
    "label": "03 / 25"
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 37,
    "width": 920,
    "height": 14,
    "label": "WHY THESE WORLDS ARE DIRECTIONS FOR CONSTRUCTION"
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 77,
    "width": 920,
    "height": 101.47999999999999,
    "label": "The means can grow.\nThe future can be made."
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 197,
    "width": 830,
    "height": 50,
    "label": "We begin with working capabilities, then ask how to connect and extend them into systems that sustain generous lives."
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 58,
    "top": 295,
    "width": 252,
    "height": 15,
    "label": "01"
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 58,
    "top": 323,
    "width": 254,
    "height": 24,
    "label": "Machinery makes machinery"
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 58,
    "top": 374,
    "width": 254,
    "height": 55.5,
    "label": "Automation already helps manufacture robots, motors, controllers, and production equipment. [E1] [E2]"
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 373,
    "top": 295,
    "width": 252,
    "height": 15,
    "label": "02"
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 373,
    "top": 323,
    "width": 254,
    "height": 24,
    "label": "Intelligence connects action"
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 373,
    "top": 374,
    "width": 254,
    "height": 55.5,
    "label": "Learned perception, planning, tool use, and robot control extend what machines can do and adapt. [E5] [E6] [E7]"
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 688,
    "top": 295,
    "width": 252,
    "height": 15,
    "label": "03"
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 688,
    "top": 323,
    "width": 254,
    "height": 24,
    "label": "Capacity expands capacity"
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 688,
    "top": 374,
    "width": 254,
    "height": 74.0,
    "label": "Some output equips new productive cells and services. Expansion can compound while inputs, maintenance, and commissioning keep pace."
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 54,
    "top": 503,
    "width": 184,
    "height": 20,
    "label": "Useful production"
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 290,
    "top": 503,
    "width": 184,
    "height": 40,
    "label": "Further productive capacity"
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 526,
    "top": 503,
    "width": 184,
    "height": 20,
    "label": "Abundant shared means"
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 762,
    "top": 503,
    "width": 184,
    "height": 20,
    "label": "Freely created worlds"
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 592,
    "width": 885,
    "height": 87,
    "label": "The purpose is a rich material life and the tools to pursue it together. Shared access can remove the need to sell labor merely to survive. People can build communities, instruments, gardens, and worlds from a foundation that keeps serving them."
  },
  {
    "page": 3,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 730,
    "width": 920,
    "height": 34,
    "label": "Full autonomous industrial reproduction remains the construction thesis. The checked evidence establishes useful pieces and a practical development path; it does not establish universal current-AI competence or a complete autonomous supply network. No doubling time is assumed."
  },
  {
    "page": 4,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 802,
    "width": 920,
    "height": 10,
    "label": "WORLDS WE CAN INHABIT / EDITION 04"
  },
  {
    "page": 4,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 920,
    "top": 802,
    "width": 40,
    "height": 10,
    "label": "04 / 25"
  },
  {
    "page": 4,
    "kind": "image",
    "x": 0,
    "top": 0,
    "width": 1000,
    "height": 666.6666666666666,
    "label": "assets/garden-district.png"
  },
  {
    "page": 4,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 681,
    "width": 920,
    "height": 14,
    "label": "THE LIVING GARDEN / ARRIVAL"
  },
  {
    "page": 4,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 706,
    "width": 345,
    "height": 64.8,
    "label": "Your city,\nyour garden"
  },
  {
    "page": 4,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 400,
    "top": 700,
    "width": 560,
    "height": 71.6,
    "label": "You arrive while breakfast is still happening. Voices travel across the water; someone waves from a table under the trees. Your home is close enough that joining can be an impulse. Shared kitchens, maintained paths, water systems, and quiet service routes support this ease. The garden is a place you can live, with room for an ordinary afternoon."
  },
  {
    "page": 5,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 802,
    "width": 920,
    "height": 10,
    "label": "WORLDS WE CAN INHABIT / EDITION 04"
  },
  {
    "page": 5,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 920,
    "top": 802,
    "width": 40,
    "height": 10,
    "label": "05 / 25"
  },
  {
    "page": 5,
    "kind": "image",
    "x": 0,
    "top": 0,
    "width": 1000,
    "height": 666.6666666666666,
    "label": "assets-v4/garden-university/garden-walk.png"
  },
  {
    "page": 5,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 681,
    "width": 920,
    "height": 14,
    "label": "THE LIVING GARDEN / INHABITATION"
  },
  {
    "page": 5,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 706,
    "width": 345,
    "height": 64.8,
    "label": "Follow the\ncooler path"
  },
  {
    "page": 5,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 400,
    "top": 700,
    "width": 560,
    "height": 71.6,
    "label": "You follow the cooler edge of the garden, where leaves move above the path. A friend stops to show you something small growing beside the water. You can linger without blocking the way. Planting, shade, seating, and accessible routes are composed together; automated care supports the landscape while people develop their own attachments to it."
  },
  {
    "page": 6,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 802,
    "width": 920,
    "height": 10,
    "label": "WORLDS WE CAN INHABIT / EDITION 04"
  },
  {
    "page": 6,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 920,
    "top": 802,
    "width": 40,
    "height": 10,
    "label": "06 / 25"
  },
  {
    "page": 6,
    "kind": "image",
    "x": 0,
    "top": 0,
    "width": 1000,
    "height": 666.6666666666666,
    "label": "assets-v4/garden-university/garden-section.png"
  },
  {
    "page": 6,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 681,
    "width": 920,
    "height": 14,
    "label": "THE LIVING GARDEN / WORKING SECTION"
  },
  {
    "page": 6,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 706,
    "width": 345,
    "height": 64.8,
    "label": "Under the\nliving landscape"
  },
  {
    "page": 6,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 400,
    "top": 700,
    "width": 560,
    "height": 89.5,
    "label": "You can trace the garden down through its roots. Terraces and rooms sit above water storage, utility routes, returned materials, and places to repair the machines that care for them. Inhabitation and maintenance have distinct paths within one structure. The landscape feels effortless because the systems beneath it have places to work, be reached, and become useful again."
  },
  {
    "page": 7,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 802,
    "width": 920,
    "height": 10,
    "label": "WORLDS WE CAN INHABIT / EDITION 04"
  },
  {
    "page": 7,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 920,
    "top": 802,
    "width": 40,
    "height": 10,
    "label": "07 / 25"
  },
  {
    "page": 7,
    "kind": "image",
    "x": 0,
    "top": 0,
    "width": 1000,
    "height": 666.6666666666666,
    "label": "assets/open-university.png"
  },
  {
    "page": 7,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 681,
    "width": 920,
    "height": 14,
    "label": "THE OPEN UNIVERSITY / ARRIVAL"
  },
  {
    "page": 7,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 706,
    "width": 345,
    "height": 64.8,
    "label": "A life gathered\naround curiosity"
  },
  {
    "page": 7,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 400,
    "top": 700,
    "width": 560,
    "height": 71.6,
    "label": "You hear a conversation before you know its subject. A table has gathered around a question, and there is space beside someone who is learning too. Across the courtyard are books, instruments, and places to make an idea tangible. Public knowledge and shared equipment give curiosity somewhere to go. You can stay an afternoon or begin a life here."
  },
  {
    "page": 8,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 802,
    "width": 920,
    "height": 10,
    "label": "WORLDS WE CAN INHABIT / EDITION 04"
  },
  {
    "page": 8,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 920,
    "top": 802,
    "width": 40,
    "height": 10,
    "label": "08 / 25"
  },
  {
    "page": 8,
    "kind": "image",
    "x": 0,
    "top": 0,
    "width": 1000,
    "height": 666.6666666666666,
    "label": "assets-v4/garden-university/university-cosmos.png"
  },
  {
    "page": 8,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 681,
    "width": 920,
    "height": 14,
    "label": "THE OPEN UNIVERSITY / SHARED INQUIRY"
  },
  {
    "page": 8,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 706,
    "width": 345,
    "height": 64.8,
    "label": "Step inside\na question"
  },
  {
    "page": 8,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 400,
    "top": 700,
    "width": 560,
    "height": 89.5,
    "label": "You stand beside friends inside a model of something too vast to encounter directly. A gesture changes the scale; a familiar point becomes a landscape of relationships. Someone asks what the model leaves out. Shared visualization, scientific instruments, and AI guidance bring difficult ideas into reach. Understanding grows through moving, questioning, and comparing what each of you notices."
  },
  {
    "page": 9,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 802,
    "width": 920,
    "height": 10,
    "label": "WORLDS WE CAN INHABIT / EDITION 04"
  },
  {
    "page": 9,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 920,
    "top": 802,
    "width": 40,
    "height": 10,
    "label": "09 / 25"
  },
  {
    "page": 9,
    "kind": "image",
    "x": 0,
    "top": 0,
    "width": 1000,
    "height": 666.6666666666666,
    "label": "assets-v4/garden-university/university-workshop.png"
  },
  {
    "page": 9,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 681,
    "width": 920,
    "height": 14,
    "label": "THE OPEN UNIVERSITY / MAKING KNOWLEDGE"
  },
  {
    "page": 9,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 706,
    "width": 345,
    "height": 64.8,
    "label": "An idea becomes\nan instrument"
  },
  {
    "page": 9,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 400,
    "top": 700,
    "width": 560,
    "height": 89.5,
    "label": "You turn a part in your hands while a more experienced visitor shows you how it connects. Nearby, a machine prepares the next piece. The question from yesterday is becoming something you can test. Shared fabrication, repair benches, and public design records let discoveries travel beyond this room. You learn enough to change the design, then leave that knowledge available."
  },
  {
    "page": 10,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 802,
    "width": 920,
    "height": 10,
    "label": "WORLDS WE CAN INHABIT / EDITION 04"
  },
  {
    "page": 10,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 920,
    "top": 802,
    "width": 40,
    "height": 10,
    "label": "10 / 25"
  },
  {
    "page": 10,
    "kind": "image",
    "x": 0,
    "top": 0,
    "width": 1000,
    "height": 666.6666666666666,
    "label": "assets-v2/exploration-community.png"
  },
  {
    "page": 10,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 681,
    "width": 920,
    "height": 14,
    "label": "THE EXPLORATION COMMUNITY / ARRIVAL"
  },
  {
    "page": 10,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 706,
    "width": 345,
    "height": 64.8,
    "label": "A dream with\na place to grow"
  },
  {
    "page": 10,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 400,
    "top": 700,
    "width": 560,
    "height": 89.5,
    "label": "You enter the spacecraft hall and instinctively lower your voice. Above the gathering, a vessel is taking shape; someone beside you recognizes a component they helped imagine. Robots and specialized tools carry out the heavy assembly. This community gives a shared dream a physical home, where learning, making, and the patient life between missions belong together."
  },
  {
    "page": 11,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 802,
    "width": 920,
    "height": 10,
    "label": "WORLDS WE CAN INHABIT / EDITION 04"
  },
  {
    "page": 11,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 920,
    "top": 802,
    "width": 40,
    "height": 10,
    "label": "11 / 25"
  },
  {
    "page": 11,
    "kind": "image",
    "x": 0,
    "top": 0,
    "width": 1000,
    "height": 666.6666666666666,
    "label": "assets-v4/exploration-quest/exploration-launch.png"
  },
  {
    "page": 11,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 681,
    "width": 920,
    "height": 14,
    "label": "THE EXPLORATION COMMUNITY / A SHARED MOMENT"
  },
  {
    "page": 11,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 706,
    "width": 345,
    "height": 64.8,
    "label": "The horizon\nopens"
  },
  {
    "page": 11,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 400,
    "top": 700,
    "width": 560,
    "height": 89.5,
    "label": "You wait with people who have followed this mission through years of questions and revisions. The distant launch lights the horizon; conversation gives way to watching. Transport, launch infrastructure, automated preparation, and a continuing flow of knowledge connect this moment to the settlement. Tomorrow, the same community will make breakfast, study what happened, and begin thinking further."
  },
  {
    "page": 12,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 802,
    "width": 920,
    "height": 10,
    "label": "WORLDS WE CAN INHABIT / EDITION 04"
  },
  {
    "page": 12,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 920,
    "top": 802,
    "width": 40,
    "height": 10,
    "label": "12 / 25"
  },
  {
    "page": 12,
    "kind": "image",
    "x": 0,
    "top": 0,
    "width": 1000,
    "height": 666.6666666666666,
    "label": "assets-v4/exploration-quest/exploration-section.png"
  },
  {
    "page": 12,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 681,
    "width": 920,
    "height": 14,
    "label": "THE EXPLORATION COMMUNITY / WORKING SECTION"
  },
  {
    "page": 12,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 706,
    "width": 345,
    "height": 64.8,
    "label": "The life behind\na mission"
  },
  {
    "page": 12,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 400,
    "top": 700,
    "width": 560,
    "height": 71.6,
    "label": "A mission has a home long before it has a launch date. You move between a public listening hall, places to learn, and views into instrument assembly. Clean work, heavy handling, and service transport have their own spaces. An observatory connects the campus to the sky. Shared knowledge and maintained equipment let the next generation continue the journey."
  },
  {
    "page": 13,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 802,
    "width": 920,
    "height": 10,
    "label": "WORLDS WE CAN INHABIT / EDITION 04"
  },
  {
    "page": 13,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 920,
    "top": 802,
    "width": 40,
    "height": 10,
    "label": "13 / 25"
  },
  {
    "page": 13,
    "kind": "image",
    "x": 0,
    "top": 0,
    "width": 1000,
    "height": 666.6666666666666,
    "label": "assets-v2/shared-quest-city.png"
  },
  {
    "page": 13,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 681,
    "width": 920,
    "height": 14,
    "label": "THE CITY OF SHARED QUESTS / ARRIVAL"
  },
  {
    "page": 13,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 706,
    "width": 345,
    "height": 64.8,
    "label": "The story\nis inhabited"
  },
  {
    "page": 13,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 400,
    "top": 700,
    "width": 560,
    "height": 71.6,
    "label": "You arrive as lanterns appear along the canal. A friend greets you in a costume they have been making all week; supper is waiting nearby. Through shared AR, the city carries creatures, histories, and invitations its residents have composed. The story continues between quests, held in real homes, workshops, friendships, and the places where people keep meeting."
  },
  {
    "page": 14,
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 40,
    "top": 802,
    "width": 920,
    "height": 10,
    "label": "WORLDS WE CAN INHABIT / EDITION 04"
  },
  {
